<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Results of <math id="S4.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\star}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\star}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> over five seeds: median running time and range, median number of branch-and-bound nodes, best objective value, dual bound, relative gap, and maximal constraint violation of the best solution.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">All instances up to <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=8</annotation></semantics></math> are solved in less than ten seconds. For <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=9</annotation></semantics></math>, the median running time is 497 seconds, about eight minutes, and the slowest of the five seeds needs about twice as long as the fastest.
Gurobi finds a configuration with the optimal value within the first 15 seconds in every seed, so almost all of the running time is spent on proving the dual bound.
The objective values exceed the exact values of Section <a href="#S6" title="6 Exact configurations for 5≤𝑛≤10 ‣ From Global Optimization to Exact Coordinates:Heilbronn’s Triangle Problem on the Unit SquareUsing Mixed-Integer Nonlinear Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> by less than <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>, as explained in Section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Setup ‣ 4 Computational study ‣ From Global Optimization to Exact Coordinates:Heilbronn’s Triangle Problem on the Unit SquareUsing Mixed-Integer Nonlinear Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>. The dual bounds exceed the exact values by at most <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.3\cdot 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.3\cdot 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.1\cdot 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.1\cdot 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> in relative terms. This corresponds to the relative gap of <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>, measured against an objective value that the feasibility tolerance slightly inflates.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Configurations with adjacent corners</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 4.3 Configurations with adjacent corners ‣ 4 Computational study ‣ From Global Optimization to Exact Coordinates:Heilbronn’s Triangle Problem on the Unit SquareUsing Mixed-Integer Nonlinear Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> reports the dual bounds of the variants for the types II and III of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Structure of optimal configurations). ‣ 2.2 Boundary structure of optimal configurations ‣ 2 Original formulation and theoretical results ‣ From Global Optimization to Exact Coordinates:Heilbronn’s Triangle Problem on the Unit SquareUsing Mixed-Integer Nonlinear Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
