<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Exact coordinates for <math id="A1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\leq n\leq 10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\leq n\leq 10</annotation></semantics></math></h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The exact coordinates of the configurations of Section <a href="#S6" title="6 Exact configurations for 5≤𝑛≤10 ‣ From Global Optimization to Exact Coordinates:Heilbronn’s Triangle Problem on the Unit SquareUsing Mixed-Integer Nonlinear Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> are listed in Tables <a href="#A1.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ Appendix A Exact coordinates for 5≤𝑛≤10 ‣ From Global Optimization to Exact Coordinates:Heilbronn’s Triangle Problem on the Unit SquareUsing Mixed-Integer Nonlinear Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, <a href="#A1.T12" title="Table 12 ‣ Appendix A Exact coordinates for 5≤𝑛≤10 ‣ From Global Optimization to Exact Coordinates:Heilbronn’s Triangle Problem on the Unit SquareUsing Mixed-Integer Nonlinear Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>, and <a href="#A1.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ Appendix A Exact coordinates for 5≤𝑛≤10 ‣ From Global Optimization to Exact Coordinates:Heilbronn’s Triangle Problem on the Unit SquareUsing Mixed-Integer Nonlinear Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>. For <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=7</annotation></semantics></math>, they are given in Table <a href="#S5.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Step 2: Exact analytical refinement ‣ 5.2 Illustration of the methodology for 𝑛=7 ‣ 5 The optimize-then-refine framework ‣ From Global Optimization to Exact Coordinates:Heilbronn’s Triangle Problem on the Unit SquareUsing Mixed-Integer Nonlinear Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
